All three functions are implemented and `python3 test_impl.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (the stress loop took 6.0s). I ran the suite after each function, and `test_impl.py` is untouched.

- **`encode`** (`rle.py`): groups consecutive characters and emits each character followed by its run length.
- **`decode`** (`rle.py`): reads each character followed by one or more digits and expands it.
- **`merge`** (`intervals.py`): sorts by start and folds each interval into the previous one when it overlaps or touches. It returns new lists and does not modify the input.

One limitation of the format itself: strings containing digit characters do not round-trip (e.g. `"1111"` encodes to `"14"`, which is ambiguous to decode). The docstrings and tests don't cover that case, so I left it.

Nothing is committed; the run also left an untracked `__pycache__/` directory.
